#document(
  default_font = "Helvetica",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter", orientation = "portrait" },
  margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) }
)

PARAGRAPH BORDERS: consecutive paragraphs with identical borders and identical side indents share one box, which holds the space between them and no rule there. A top or bottom border adds its space and its width to the height of a paragraph.

The paragraph before the boxes.

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1.5), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(6) } })[The first of two paragraphs with identical borders.]

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1.5), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(6) } })[The second of two paragraphs with identical borders.]

The paragraph between the boxes.

#paragraph(fill = "#fff4e5", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(2), color = "#b45309", space = pt(8) } })[A single paragraph with a border eight points from its text.]

The paragraph after the single box.

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1.5), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(6) } })[A paragraph with a blue border.]

#paragraph(fill = "#fff4e5", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1.5), color = "#b45309", space = pt(6) } })[A paragraph with a border of another colour.]

The paragraph after the boxes.

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[The first of three paragraphs in one box.]

#paragraph(border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[The second of three paragraphs in one box, without a fill.]

#paragraph(fill = "#fff4e5", alignment = "center", spacing = { before = pt(12), after = pt(3) }, indent = { first_line = pt(20) }, border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[The third of three paragraphs in one box, with spacing of its own.]

The paragraph after the box of three.

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[A paragraph with a box at the margin.]

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", indent = { left = pt(20) }, border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[A paragraph with an identical border and another left indent.]

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", indent = { left = pt(20), right = pt(20) }, border = { all = { style = "single", width = pt(1), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[A paragraph with an identical border and another right indent.]

The paragraph after the indented boxes.

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { left = { style = "single", width = pt(3), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[The first of two paragraphs with a rule on the left.]

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { left = { style = "single", width = pt(3), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) } })[The second of two paragraphs with a rule on the left.]

#paragraph(fill = "#eef4ff", border = { left = { style = "single", width = pt(3), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(4) }, bottom = { style = "single", width = pt(2), color = "#2563eb", space = pt(6) } })[A paragraph with a further rule below.]

The last paragraph.
